IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `taa-instalments`

-- Taxation Administration Act 1953, Schedule 1 Division 45, s 45-80 and Part IIA ss 8AAC, 8AAD -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_taxation-administration-act-1953_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Facts from the WA lives (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-*): Chloe turns 15 on 14 March 2018 and takes a casual job
-- at a supermarket (c020); her first graduate payslip on 29 February 2024 is $5,833.33 for the month (c041). Daniel turns 16 on
-- 15 October 2012 with a TFN and a casual job (d012). Jake turns 15 on 30 August 2021 with a TFN and no job (k020); on 20 October
-- 2028 he lodges his first return as a sole trader on $31,000, not registered for GST (k043). Daniel founds the Rossi
-- Foundation, a private ancillary fund, on 1 March 2051 and gives it $2,000,000 (d072); on 3 May 2076 its trustee company passes
-- to his children (d091).
-- Figures the scenarios do not give are the encoder's, HYPOTHETICAL, and labelled where used. The text encoded is the 2026
-- compilation, not the law as it stood in 2012 or 2018, or as it will stand in 2051 or 2076.

-- k043 assumptions, HYPOTHETICAL: notional tax 2,500; an 8% rate given on 15 November 2028; instalment income 7,750 (a quarter of
-- $31,000); a base interest rate of 3.95%.

`k043: Jake, a sole trader, makes no choice` MEANS `Me as an instalment payer` WITH
    `I meet the monthly payer requirement` IS FALSE
    `I am registered or required to be registered for GST` IS FALSE
    `I am a partner in a GST-registered partnership` IS FALSE
    `my most recent notional tax notified` IS 2500
    `I choose to pay annually` IS FALSE
    `I choose to pay on my instalment income` IS FALSE
    `I am a primary producer with a base-year profit from it` IS FALSE
    `I am a special professional with a base-year profit from it` IS FALSE

`k043: Jake chooses to pay annually` MEANS `Me as an instalment payer` WITH
    `I meet the monthly payer requirement` IS FALSE
    `I am registered or required to be registered for GST` IS FALSE
    `I am a partner in a GST-registered partnership` IS FALSE
    `my most recent notional tax notified` IS 2500
    `I choose to pay annually` IS TRUE
    `I choose to pay on my instalment income` IS FALSE
    `I am a primary producer with a base-year profit from it` IS FALSE
    `I am a special professional with a base-year profit from it` IS FALSE

`k043: Jake chooses to pay annually but his notional tax is 9000` MEANS `Me as an instalment payer` WITH
    `I meet the monthly payer requirement` IS FALSE
    `I am registered or required to be registered for GST` IS FALSE
    `I am a partner in a GST-registered partnership` IS FALSE
    `my most recent notional tax notified` IS 9000
    `I choose to pay annually` IS TRUE
    `I choose to pay on my instalment income` IS FALSE
    `I am a primary producer with a base-year profit from it` IS FALSE
    `I am a special professional with a base-year profit from it` IS FALSE

`a farmer whose base-year farm income exceeded its deductions` MEANS `Me as an instalment payer` WITH
    `I meet the monthly payer requirement` IS FALSE
    `I am registered or required to be registered for GST` IS FALSE
    `I am a partner in a GST-registered partnership` IS FALSE
    `my most recent notional tax notified` IS 2500
    `I choose to pay annually` IS FALSE
    `I choose to pay on my instalment income` IS FALSE
    `I am a primary producer with a base-year profit from it` IS TRUE
    `I am a special professional with a base-year profit from it` IS FALSE

§ `ss 45-15, 45-50(4)`

-- c041: Chloe, on wages alone, is given no rate and is not liable. k043: Jake is liable only once the Commissioner gives
-- him a rate; his business income alone does not make him liable.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I liable to pay PAYG instalments` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I liable to pay PAYG instalments` TRUE FALSE

§ `s 45-140`

-- k043: not registered for GST; notional tax of 2,500 is less than $8,000; 8,000 is not.
#ASSERT `May I choose to pay annually` FALSE FALSE 2500
#ASSERT NOT `May I choose to pay annually` FALSE FALSE 8000

§ `ss 45-125, 45-130, 45-132, 45-134`

#ASSERT `What kind of instalment payer am I` `k043: Jake, a sole trader, makes no choice` EQUALS `a quarterly payer paying 4 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax`
#ASSERT `What kind of instalment payer am I` `k043: Jake chooses to pay annually` EQUALS `an annual payer`
#ASSERT `What kind of instalment payer am I` `k043: Jake chooses to pay annually but his notional tax is 9000` EQUALS `a quarterly payer paying 4 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax`
#ASSERT `What kind of instalment payer am I` `a farmer whose base-year farm income exceeded its deductions` EQUALS `a quarterly payer paying 2 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax`

§ `ss 45-50, 45-125(2)`

-- k043: a rate first given on 15 November 2028 starts in the October-December quarter; nothing is due for July-September.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I liable for an instalment for the quarter` `a quarterly payer paying 4 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax` 2029 1 TRUE (Date 15 11 2028) FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I liable for an instalment for the quarter` `a quarterly payer paying 4 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax` 2029 2 TRUE (Date 15 11 2028) FALSE

§ `ss 45-61, 45-70`

-- k043: the October-December 2028 instalment is due 21 January 2029, or 28 February 2029 as a deferred BAS payer; an annual
-- instalment for 2028-29 on 21 October 2029.
#ASSERT `By when must I pay my quarterly instalment` 2029 2 FALSE EQUALS (Date 21 1 2029)
#ASSERT `By when must I pay my quarterly instalment` 2029 2 TRUE EQUALS (Date 28 2 2029)

#ASSERT `By when must I pay my annual instalment` 2029 EQUALS (Date 21 10 2029)

§ `ss 45-1, 45-110`

-- A rate he chooses (5%) displaces the Commissioner's 8%. On instalment income of 7,750 at 8%: 620 (INFERENCE from s 45-1).
#ASSERT `What instalment rate applies to me` 8 TRUE 5 EQUALS 5

#ASSERT `How much is my quarterly instalment` 7750 8 EQUALS 620

§ `ss 45-20, 45-30`

-- k043: on GDP-adjusted notional tax he need not notify his instalment income; on instalment income he must.
#ASSERT NOT `Must I notify my instalment income` `a quarterly payer paying 4 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax` FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I notify my instalment income` `a quarterly payer on instalment income` FALSE

#ASSERT `What credit do I get for my instalments` 2480 0 TRUE EQUALS 2480

§ `s 45-80; ss 8AAC, 8AAD`

-- k043: base rate 3.95% + 7 = 10.95% a year, / 365 = 0.03% a day. 620 unpaid for 30 days, compounding daily:
-- 620 x (1.0003^30 - 1) = 5.604..., shown as 5.60 (simple interest would be 5.58).
#ASSERT `What is the daily general interest charge rate` 3.95 365 EQUALS 0.03

#ASSERT `How much general interest charge do I owe` 620 3.95 365 30 EQUALS 5.6

